<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40277" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quō-nam</span></b> , adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Whither pray?</i> (class.): quo tu te agis? <i>Char.</i> Quonam, nisi domum? <i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Trin. 4, 3, 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Merc. 5, 2, 16</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eam si nunc sequor, quonam?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 8, 3, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quonam haec omnia, nisi ad suam perniciem
					pertinere?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 1, 9, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>How far pray?</i> quonam usque? <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 1,
				215</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 511</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id.
				Achill. 1, 624</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 1, 3, 19</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
